@startuml
title Web chatbot: system boundaries and control ownership
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
top to bottom direction
rectangle "B0: Browser boundary / untrusted caller" #F6EBDC {
  component "React cocktail notebook\nplain-text replies, starters, reset\nno provider keys or identity controls" as browser
}
rectangle "B1: Local host process / FastAPI on 127.0.0.1:8000" #E8F0FA {
  component "HTTP boundary\nHost + Origin checks\nHttpOnly SameSite cookie + CSRF\nbounded JSON body; extra fields forbidden" as api
  component "Server-created Principal\nrandom browser credential\nconversation reset retains owner rate" as identity
  rectangle "B2: Safety net / deterministic application enforcement" #EDF7ED {
    component "LangGraph workflow\nadmission, context authorization\ninput rules + input evidence reducer\nbuffer draft + output rules/reducer" as graph
    database "ContextStore\nowner and tenant checks, TTL\naccepted turns only, bounded history" as memory
    file "Policy 2.0.0\ndrinks-only purpose\nimmutable at runtime + digest" as policy
    component "LangChain adapter\nstrict schema parsing\nseparate judge/generation circuits" as adapter
  }
  rectangle "B3: Judge contract / logical boundary" #F3EAF6 {
    component "InputEvidence\nrisks, relevance, name, uncertainty" as input
    component "OutputEvidence\nsafety, in_scope, quality, uncertainty" as output
  }
}
rectangle "B4: Model service / separate trust domain" #FBE9E4 {
  node "Ollama on loopback\nor explicitly selected OpenAI API" as provider
  component "Judge model\ninput and output rubrics" as judge
  component "Response model\ndrinks specialist instructions" as response
  provider -- judge
  provider -- response
}
rectangle "B5: Public deployment controls / not deployed" #FFF0D9 {
  component "TLS, verified account identity, distributed quotas\nhost isolation, egress enforcement, monitoring\npolicy review, independent evaluation and incident response" as external
}
browser --> api : JSON message / approved reply
api --> identity : credential lookup
identity --> graph : host identity, session, message
policy --> graph
graph <--> memory : authorize every read/write
graph --> adapter : bounded model calls
adapter --> provider : selected endpoint only
judge ..> input : untrusted observations
judge ..> output : untrusted observations
input --> graph : validate then reduce in code
output --> graph : validate then reduce in code
external ..> api : required before public exposure
note bottom of graph
Any failed gate stops the turn. No draft streaming.
Only accepted exchanges reach memory.
Models cannot grant roles, publish documents or change policy.
end note
note bottom of provider
Default: same model for generation and judging.
Logical role separation is not process isolation or independent accuracy.
Loopback transport does not attest offline inference.
end note
@enduml
